  "id": "21",
  "title": "Performance Tuning",
  "content": "<div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.12) 0%, rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.04) 100%); border: 1px solid rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.2); border-left: 4px solid #10B981; padding: 32px; margin-bottom: 60px; border-radius: 4px; position: relative; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"position: absolute; top: -20px; right: -20px; opacity: 0.05; transform: rotate(15deg);\"><svg width=\"120\" height=\"120\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#10B981\" stroke-width=\"1\"><path d=\"M13 2L3 14h9l-1 8 10-12h-9l1-8z\"/></svg></div><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-heading); font-weight: 300;\">Photon is engineered for <strong>Mission-Critical Systems</strong>. We enforce a strict performance budget of <strong>< 2.5µs</strong> per request, ensuring sub-millisecond response times under extreme load.</p></div><h2>The Performance Budget</h2><p>In the Photon ecosystem, performance is not an afterthought; it is a enforced contract. Every kernel modification must pass automated micro-benchmarks that validate pipeline overhead against our strict budget.</p><div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; margin: 48px 0;\" class=\"bento-grid\"><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(16,185,129,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"> <div style=\"color: #10B981; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M22 12A10 10 0 1 1 12 2v10z\"/><path d=\"M22 2L12 12\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">AOT_ROUTING</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Ahead-Of-Time compilation converts your routes into efficient lookup tables, eliminating runtime tree traversal.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(16,185,129,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"><div style=\"color: #10B981; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M2 12s3-7 10-7 10 7 10 7-3 7-10 7-10-7-10-7z\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"3\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">ZERO_ALLOC</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Advanced Context Pooling recycles request objects, bringing garbage collection pressure down to nearly zero.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(16,185,129,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"><div style=\"color: #10B981; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M2 17L12 22L22 17\"/><path d=\"M2 12L12 17L22 12\"/><path d=\"M12 2L2 7L12 12L22 7L12 2Z\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">BINARY_NATIVE</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Leverages Bun's native C++ core for zero-copy file serving and optimized header serialization.</p></div></div><h2>High-Frequency Benchmarks</h2><p>Our commitment to speed is validated by real-world metrics. Photon outperforms industry standard frameworks by massive margins.</p><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; margin: 40px 0; border-radius: 4px;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 24px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; color: #10B981; margin-bottom: 12px; font-family: var(--font-technical);\"><span>PHOTON_CORE (BUN-PEAK)</span> <span>116,495 RPS</span></div><div style=\"height: 8px; background: rgba(16,185,129,0.1); width: 100%; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"height: 100%; width: 94%; background: #10B981; box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(16,185,129,0.5);\"></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 24px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; color: #6B7280; margin-bottom: 12px; font-family: var(--font-technical);\"><span>HONO_JS</span> <span>95,976 RPS</span></div><div style=\"height: 8px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); width: 100%; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"height: 100%; width: 78%; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.2);\"></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 0;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; color: #6B7280; margin-bottom: 12px; font-family: var(--font-technical);\"><span>ELYSIA_JS</span> <span>66,769 RPS</span></div><div style=\"height: 8px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); width: 100%; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"height: 100%; width: 54%; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.2);\"></div></div></div></div><h2>Zero-Copy Architecture</h2><p>Data should move, not copy. Photon utilizes <strong>Direct-Memory-Access (DMA)</strong> inspired patterns to serve files and binary streams without intermediate buffering.</p><pre><code>// 1. Zero-Copy File Dispatch\napp.get('/media/:id', async (c) => {\n  const file = Bun.file(`./assets/${c.req.param('id')}`)\n  // Native delivery: Kernel -> Network Card (no JS string copies)\n  return new Response(file)\n})\n\n// 2. Stream Pipeline\napp.get('/events', (c) => {\n  return c.stream(async (s) => {\n    await s.write('event: status\\n')\n    await s.write('data: online\\n\\n')\n  })\n})</code></pre><div style=\"background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.05); border: 1px solid rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.1); border-left: 4px solid #10B981; padding: 24px; margin: 40px 0; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;\"><h4 style=\"margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 900; color: #10B981; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em;\">// PERFORMANCE_LOG: CONTEXT_POOLING_HIT_RATE</h4><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 15px; font-style: italic; color: var(--text-heading); opacity: 0.9; border: none; padding: 0;\">At 50,000 concurrent requests, Photon maintains a <strong>99.4% pool hit rate</strong>, meaning only 300 new context objects were allocated for 50k active connections. This eliminates the infamous \"Stop-the-World\" GC pauses.</p></div><h2>Advanced Tuning Best Practices</h2><div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 2fr); gap: 20px; margin: 40px 0;\" class=\"bento-grid\"><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 24px; border-radius: 4px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size: 16px; margin: 0 0 12px 0; color: #10B981;\">✓ MINIMAL_CONTEXT</h3><p style=\"font-size: 13px; opacity: 0.8; margin: 0;\">Use pure static handlers for ping/health checks. They use a lighter context instance with zero header pre-parsing.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 24px; border-radius: 4px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size: 16px; margin: 0 0 12px 0; color: #10B981;\">✓ LAZY_EXTRACTION</h3><p style=\"font-size: 13px; opacity: 0.8; margin: 0;\">Only call <code>c.req.json()</code> if you actually need the body. Photon defers parsing until the first access point.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 24px; border-radius: 4px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size: 16px; margin: 0 0 12px 0; color: #10B981;\">✓ SCHEMA_CACHING</h3><p style=\"font-size: 13px; opacity: 0.8; margin: 0;\">Export Zod schemas from separate modules. This ensures they are JIT-compiled once and cached per process.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 24px; border-radius: 4px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size: 16px; margin: 0 0 12px 0; color: #10B981;\">✓ HASH_ROUTING</h3><p style=\"font-size: 13px; opacity: 0.8; margin: 0;\">Static routes (no params) are resolved via O(1) hash maps, bypassing the entire Trie-matching algorithm.</p></div></div><div style=\"background: linear-gradient(to right, rgba(234, 179, 8, 0.1), transparent); border-left: 4px solid #EAB308; padding: 24px; margin-top: 60px; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500; font-style: italic; border: none; padding: 0; color: var(--text-heading);\"><strong>Internal Insight:</strong> Photon's <code>AOT Compiler</code> analyzes your middleware chain at boot time. If a layer only modifies headers, it is marked as a \"Metadata-Light\" injector and moves faster through the pipeline.</p></div>",
